8. Formal Definition of “Continuous Structural Awareness”

Continuous Structural Awareness (CSA) is the property of a structural digital twin system whereby the state‑space representation of the structure is updated at a temporal frequency equal to or greater than the characteristic time‑constant of the fastest damage‑progression mode being monitored. For a Starship booster, the fastest relevant crack‑growth mode (cryogenic‑thermal‑cycle‑driven fatigue in SS304) has a characteristic propagation rate of ~0.01 mm per full cryo‑ambient cycle, so CSA requires that the digital twin detect a 0.02 mm change before the next flight. This differs from existing continuous‑monitoring frameworks in the SHM literature, which typically assume permanently affixed sensor networks and do not address the swarm‑acquired, non‑permanent sensor‑deployment paradigm.

